quran[15]{c,v,t}:
  50,1,"Qaf, by the Glorious Qur’an."
  50,2,"Rather, they are astonished that a Warner has come to them from among themselves. So the disbelievers say: ‘This is a strange thing!"
  50,3,What! When we are dead and have become dust (then we shall be raised again)? Such return is far-fetched (i.e. impossible to perceive).’
  50,4,We surely know what the earth consumes of them (i.e. their bodies after death). And with Us is an all-preserving Book.
  50,5,"Rather, they reject the truth when it has come to them. So, they are in a state of confusion."
  50,6,"Do they not look at the heavenly universe above them, how We built it and decorated it (with galaxies, stars and planets), and there are no cracks (or defects) in it?"
  50,7,"As for the earth, We spread it out and cast in it firm mountains and caused every pleasant kind of plant to grow in it."
  50,8,"(In this, there is) an insight and a reminder for every penitent servant."
  50,9,"And We send down blessed rainwater from the sky, whereby We grow gardens and grain for harvest."
  50,10,"And tall date palms loaded with clusters of fruits,"
  50,11,"as a provision for the servants. And with it, We revive a dead land. Likewise shall be the emergence (from the graves)."
  50,12,"Before them, the people of Nuh (Noah) denied (the truth), and so did the inhabitants of the blind well (al-Rass in Yamama) and Thamud (the people of Salih, in the town of al-Hijr near Tabuk)."
  50,13,"So did ‘Ad (the people of Hud in the Ahqaf valley of Yemen), Pharaoh (the ruler of Egypt) and the people of Lut (Lot, living in Sodom and ‘Amura [Gomorrah] in Palestine)."
  50,14,"So did the inhabitants of al-Ayka (the forest-dwellers of Madyan, i.e. the people of Shu‘ayb) and the people of Tubba‘ (As‘ad Abu Karib al-Himyari, the King of Yemen). All of them rejected the messengers. So, My promise of punishment (against them) proved true."
  50,15,"Did We get exhausted with the first creation? Instead, they are in doubt regarding (their) new creation."
